  title: Queuing Culture - 1960s
  info: "As Singapore modernized, queuing became an unspoken rule in public spaces.
    Whether at hawker centers, bus stops, or theme parks, Singaporeans diligently
    form lines and wait their turn. This social norm reflects the nation\u2019s emphasis
    on order and efficiency.  "
